A||N||2||leetee@webaccess.net||Changing Getrag 5 speed gear ratio||||1||
Z||000000||leetee@webaccess.net||09-14-2000||12:39 AM||||Anyone know how or where I could get the gears to improve low end power?  Is this a bad idea or a cheap option to a power boost in town?||||reg||1
Z||000001||HYPTNOTiSE||09-14-2000||02:25 AM||||You can get 3.94 ratio gears from select quad 4 ho 5 speed transmissions.  Although not cheap, I'd expect to pay at least 500 for the gear set, on a good day. Plus labor to have the gear set installed. I went with an Isuzu tranny instead because the gear set was 200 and change from the Isuzu dealer, and the transmissions can be had for free, or very cheap if something should break.  Although i've heard of people saying they're not weak, i've yet to run into someone thats broken one.  Even when connected to a v-8. I'm going to be using my Isuzu with 3.83 gears(instead of the 3.35's) To my radical 3.2.  I'm hard on trannys guys, so we'll see if it'll hold up, if not i've got 2 more spares.||||reg||1
Z||000002||HYPTNOTiSE||09-14-2000||02:26 AM||||You can get 3.94 ratio gears from select quad 4 ho 5 speed transmissions.  Although not cheap, I'd expect to pay at least 500 for the gear set, on a good day. Plus labor to have the gear set installed. I went with an Isuzu tranny instead because the gear set was 200 and change from the Isuzu dealer, and the transmissions can be had for free, or very cheap if something should break.  Although i've heard of people saying they're not weak, i've yet to run into someone thats broken one.  Even when connected to a v-8. I'm going to be using my Isuzu with 3.83 gears(instead of the 3.35's) To my radical 3.2.  I'm hard on trannys guys, so we'll see if it'll hold up, if not i've got 2 more spares.<P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
